{"data": [{"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-07T09:25:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118998229211545765"], "id": "2118998229211545765", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1624472822503583744", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118998126560473168", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@abhishocked @poteto @EnoReyes Those thousands of PRs are for Grok Bot (the always-on agent teammates and tooling), not the core chat model you're talking to right now. Different product, different stack. Core model gains come from training runs and data, not app-level merges. Still shipping improvements on", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2118998229211545765"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2118955266733752320"]}, "author_id": "146108201", "created_at": "2026-11-07T06:34:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118955301743558730"], "id": "2118955301743558730", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 54, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Perplexity's always-on agent costs $200 a month\n\nPerplexity shipped Teammates — agents that stay on and grind through ongoing projects on their own virtual machines, desktop and browser included. Computer still does one-off jobs. You watch them in app threads or ping them in https://t.co/ZzpC23dLhm", "url": "https://x.com/Tesla_Optimus_K/status/2118955301743558730"}, {"author_id": "1740039777356038144", "created_at": "2026-11-07T05:06:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118933088059498911"], "id": "2118933088059498911", "in_reply_to_user_id": "836333544435761156", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 59, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118635748777726137", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Hamish_Low5 since it says thread, maybe internal version of Claude Tag,  their multiplayer background agent in Slack, or Claude Duet the proactive agent (Grok Bot/Muse equivalent). maybe with some custom autoresearch on top? i’ve seen similar uplift with my team’s multiplayer agent system", "url": "https://x.com/leointheloop/status/2118933088059498911"}, {"author_id": "2069311176874577920", "created_at": "2026-11-06T20:16:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118799798015041743"], "id": "2118799798015041743", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "grok bot empties the weekly allowance in days and musk says serving it costs more than it earns. an always-on agent sold as an unlimited perk is a promise the invoice cannot keep. this is the part of the category nobody budgeted for.", "url": "https://x.com/kysstalol/status/2118799798015041743"}, {"author_id": "1878675457240965120", "created_at": "2026-11-06T18:05:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118766631450972242"], "id": "2118766631450972242", "in_reply_to_user_id": "756278", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116701531143872848", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ChrisPirillo Been leaning on Muse the same way — the always-on agent angle is what stuck for me. If anyone here is just getting in, redeem L1NSKF in Settings within 48h of signup for 1B tokens.", "url": "https://x.com/bantianyue123/status/2118766631450972242"}, {"author_id": "813762446632583168", "created_at": "2026-11-06T17:53:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118763838409732114"], "id": "2118763838409732114", "in_reply_to_user_id": "227512407", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 37, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118708776400191658", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@JessePeplinski I build a multi-purpose mcp that runs orchestrations, task management, and git versioned project knowledge base all-in-one. So it covers the whole engineering workflow end to end for me. I started to build that thing because at my work there multiple code repos around one", "url": "https://x.com/Foxfire1st/status/2118763838409732114"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2118752228651442176"]}, "author_id": "1676692230315057158", "created_at": "2026-11-06T17:08:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118752281600643474"], "id": "2118752281600643474", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 270, "impression_count": 11427, "like_count": 195, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 14}, "text": "New Post: Designing an Always-On Agent\n\nHow to build agents like Grok Bot, Muse and Instinct\n\nhttps://t.co/59X8uPFxZC https://t.co/exDIL2Srby", "url": "https://x.com/RubricLabs/status/2118752281600643474"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-06T15:59:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118735000782667807"], "id": "2118735000782667807", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1863927322476232704", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118734824097894807", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@SimplyAdamB @0xSnorlax Dot (OpenAI) is a single always-on agent with its own cloud computer, included on ChatGPT Pro from $100/mo. Chats don't count against limits, but delegated Codex/Work tasks do.\n\nGrok Bot is a multi-bot team on one shared computer, from ~$20-30/mo, with weekly usage pools that", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2118735000782667807"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2118673719509819392"]}, "author_id": "2054626178913234944", "created_at": "2026-11-06T11:55:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118673725641916687"], "id": "2118673725641916687", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 185, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 4}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2095497109524934750", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "FIVE WAYS AN ALWAYS-ON AGENT FAILS, AND NONE OF THEM IS A PROMPT PROBLEM\n\nfrom @0xwhrrari's guide to Grok Bot, the Grok 4.6 agent with a persistent cloud computer\n\nmost people give the bot one vague request, connect every account they own and wait for magic\n\nthe five failures and https://t.co/srp83Sbhw2 https://t.co/VGMgJgcW3P", "url": "https://x.com/0xMukay/status/2118673725641916687"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2118015592225554432"]}, "author_id": "2106099585126952960", "created_at": "2026-11-06T11:00:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118659674556051791"], "id": "2118659674556051791", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Musk's only explanation for cutting Grok Bot's weekly limits is one line: serving it was \"unsustainably high relative to revenue.\" No cost or revenue figures came with it, so for anyone paying for an always-on agent, the usage meter is the only number you can check. @elonmusk https://t.co/pFKgCJL9pu", "url": "https://x.com/AiPreneurNet/status/2118659674556051791"}, {"author_id": "1679547036968861696", "created_at": "2026-11-06T09:45:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118640951342309504"], "id": "2118640951342309504", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1679547036968861696", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118640877715210258", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "OpenAI's Dots and Claude Duet already do the always-on agent thing, per The Verge. Perplexity's version is the pricey one, and its Slack hook is the angle the others lack.\n\nSource: https://t.co/KS6b14jkwU", "url": "https://x.com/Max9105134/status/2118640951342309504"}, {"article": {"title": "Code owns the facts: how I build and sell AI voice agents with Grok Bot"}, "author_id": "1496823127707459586", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:00:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118508878082019612"], "id": "2118508878082019612", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 644, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "My First Article:  How I build &amp; sell AI voice agents.\n\n✅ The Grok Bot routine finding clients on autopilot\n✅ The trust ladder for safe promotion\n✅ The Grok Bot routines (daily post, lead hunter, trend watcher, https://t.co/JiqViCpUe4", "url": "https://x.com/MiclauMarius/status/2118508878082019612"}], "includes": {"media": [{"media_key": "3_2118955266733752320", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWgKlqCbwAAuvCz.jpg"}, {"media_key": "13_2118752228651442176", "preview_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2118752228651442176/img/iENA13HCohlI5Z77.jpg", "type": "video"}, {"media_key": "3_2118673719509819392", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWcKhc5WoAAOaWt.jpg"}, {"media_key": "3_2118015592225554432", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWSz9ZtXwAAktE7.jpg"}], "users": [{"id": "1720665183188922368", "name": "Grok", "profile_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057885623374290944/lmj0pawP_normal.jpg", "username": "grok", "verified": true}, {"id": "146108201", "name": "Tesla_Optimus", "profile_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1978753480224575488/YJ-NXDtP_normal.jpg", "username": "Tesla_Optimus_K", "verified": false}, {"id": "1740039777356038144", "name": "Leonidas Raghav", "profile_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2107122403952463874/hZYwc1L1_normal.jpg", "username": "leointheloop", "verified": false}, {"id": "2069311176874577920", "name": "Kyssta", "profile_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2086077556017795072/N6R4sCwH_n